      "writtenOn": "2024-09-18T17:18:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My understanding is that `mc.flags` and `gfp` are different types.\n\n`mc.flags` defines the following bits\n\n```\n#define HYP_MEMCACHE_ACCOUNT_KMEMCG BIT(1)\n#define HYP_MEMCACHE_ACCOUNT_STAGE2 BIT(2)\n```\n\nThe function `hyp_mc_alloc_fn` provides a mapping from `mc.flags` to `gfp` flags. It doesn\u0027t just pass `mc.flags` directly into `__get_free_pages`.\n\nIf I\u0027m not mistaken, this change does not achieve the desired result.\n\nShould we add something like\n```\n#define HYP_MEMCACHE_GFP_ATOMIC BIT(3)\n```",
      "revId": "75f52c6fe54cb76cbd33d3bbfc65cfcf95e76435",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
